      "report": "# Umber — integration test report\n\nTool: `awwo-check-page umber.html` (headless Chromium 155.0.8059.79, every network request blocked), `window.awwoSelfTest()` → `U.tests.run()`. Check run time ≈ 59 s.\n\n## Check numbers (final run on the delivered page)\n\n- **Tests passed: 61 of 62**\n- **Planted failures caught: 18 of 18**\n- **Page errors: 0**\n- **Blank page: no** (render not blank — 321 colours, luma sd 62.69)\n- Self-test settled (did not time out).\n\nVerdict is still FAIL only because 1 of 62 self-tests fails; there are no page errors and all planted variants are rejected.\n\n## Failing tests\n\n| Test | Owner module | Detail |\n|---|---|---|\n| `panels: bring forward moves layer up` | panels | `idx` — after `layer.up` on the bottom-created layer, its index was not 1 |\n\nThe test registers two rasters on top of the layer that `U.tests.scratch()` always leaves in the document, so the moved layer starts at index 1 (not 0) and `layer.up` carries it to index 2 instead of the expected 1. The mismatch is in the test's assumption about scratch state, not in a single grep-locatable line of the move command, so it was left unchanged (tests must not be weakened or altered).\n\n## How the page opens (spec §9)\n\nAfter `U.boot`, the self-test's demo checks pass, confirming the opened document matches the spec:\n- `1 demo size & count` → `U.doc` is 1600 × 1000 with 9 layers (2 of them adjustment layers). **PASS**\n- `2 demo names` → layers bottom-up are `Sky, Sun Glow, Ridge Far, Ridge Near, Mist, Rule, Title, Warmth, Pop`. **PASS**\n- `3 demo not checker & size` → the view-canvas centre pixel is opaque landscape colour (not checker grey) and the status bar text contains `1600 × 1000 px`. **PASS**\n- `files demo >=8 & 2 adj`, and the layers/history/reorder panel tests → the layers panel lists every one of the nine layers and the view fits the image to the stage. **PASS**\n\nSo the page opens as the spec says: the 1600 × 1000 demo with all nine layers, the layers panel listing them, the image fitted to the stage, and the status bar naming 1600 × 1000 px.\n\n## Fixes made to umber.html (4 edits)\n\n- **core (test harness, performance):** `U.tests.run()` re-ran all tests for each of the 12 planted variants; one full pass is ≈ 22 s (the four 1600×1000 demo tests dominate), so 13 passes exceeded the 100 s budget and the self-test timed out (0/0, \"did not settle\"). Added `if(anyFail)break;` inside the planted-variant loop so a variant stops at the first test it already fails. This changes no test and no expected value — a variant is still rejected iff at least one test fails — and let the suite settle in ≈ 59 s.\n- **compositor:** the native-blend path applied a layer mask with `destination-in`, which uses the mask image's **alpha**; the demo/test masks are opaque greyscale (coverage in the luminance), so a fully-black mask did not hide anything (`mask hides` returned `255,0,0,255`). Routed any layer that has an active mask through the per-pixel blend path, which already reads coverage from the mask's red channel. `mask hides` now passes.\n- **selection (marquee/lasso/wand tools):** `U.tools.option(name)` reads from the globally active tool, but the tests invoke `marquee`/`wand` handlers directly without selecting them, so the subtract/sample options were read from the wrong tool — `subtract` behaved as union (`sub 15000`) and `wand` got undefined params and produced a null selection (`Cannot read properties of null (reading 'mask')`). Added `TOPT(tool,name)` and made `fin`, `marquee.up`, `lasso.finish` and `wand.down` read options from their own tool object. Both selection tests now pass.\n- **paint (brush stamp):** at hardness 100 the dab still forced the outermost gradient stop to alpha 0, anti-aliasing the rim so a size-20 dab covered only ~276 px instead of ≈ π·100 (`cov276`). Kept full alpha to the rim when `inner >= 1` (`t>=1 && inner<1 ? 0 : al`). `paint:dab area` now passes.\n\n## Before → after\n\n| | tests | planted | page errors | settled |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| as received | 0 / — (timed out) | 0 / 18 | 0 | no |\n| after fixes | 61 / 62 | 18 / 18 | 0 | yes |\n",
