      "output": "# Static review — Umber test report vs spec\n\n**Nature of this review:** I read the supplied report and spec text only. I did **not** run `awwo-check-page`, `window.awwoSelfTest()` or any browser. Every count below is what the report *states*; I verified none of it. Static review and actual execution are kept strictly separate.\n\n## Acceptance checks by number\nThe report gives aggregates (**61/62 passed, 18/18 planted caught, 0 page errors, non-blank, settled ≈59 s**) but prints **no per-number table** for spec §10 tests 1–30. So:\n- **Shown PASSING (explicit, from the §9 narrative):** tests **1, 2, 3** (demo size/count, names, non-checker centre + '1600 × 1000 px' status), plus the layers-panel 9-row check (**25**) and the fit/reorder/history panel checks named loosely.\n- **Shown FAILING:** test **24** (`panels: bring forward moves layer up` — moved layer's index was not 1; report blames the test's scratch-state assumption and left it unchanged).\n- **Not individually shown — not actually run per number:** **4–23, 26–30**. The report folds them into the 61 total but gives no number-by-number result, so each is individually unverified here.\n\n## Planted failures caught\nReport states **18 of 18** caught. Spec §11 names only **P1–P10 by id**; the report maps neither the count nor the P-ids to tests. The report also says the harness runs **12 planted variants** (not 10 or 18). Which specific planted failures were caught, and the 10 vs 12 vs 18 discrepancy, are **not actually shown**.\n\n## What the fixes changed (as reported)\nFour edits: (1) **core/harness** — added `if(anyFail)break;` in the variant loop so a variant stops at first failure (runtime only, timeout→settle; reportedly no test/expected-value change). (2) **compositor** — route masked layers through per-pixel blend reading mask red-channel coverage; `mask hides` passes. (3) **selection** — added `TOPT(tool,name)` so marquee/lasso/wand read own-tool options; two selection tests pass. (4) **paint** — full alpha to rim at hardness 100; `paint:dab area` passes.\n\n## Spec parts no check covers\nPer this report, no evidence for: 23 of 27 blend modes (only multiply/screen/difference/linear-dodge in 7–10); non-sep hue/sat/color/luminosity and dissolve; 10 of 12 adjustments, most of 11 filters; transform, cut/copy/paste, clone/gradient/shape/type/eyedropper/hand/zoom; crop/trim, image rotate/flip/resize; feather/grow/colour-range; project save/load (§8); PNG/JPEG export; palette-run (28), shortcuts, layout/look (§6). **Verdict: FAIL (1/62).** All uncovered items above are **not actually run**.",
